+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Repository support
+
+- [x] 1.1 Add `OrderRepository.applyCoupon(id, discountCents, finalAmountCents, couponCode)` that updates the order row; verify with a unit-level repository check that the stored order reflects the new values
+- [x] 1.2 Add `CouponRepository.insertRedemption(orderId, code, discountCents, createdAt)` and `CouponRepository.incrementUsedCount(code)`; verify a redemption row is inserted and `usedCount` increases
+
+## 2. Service rules
+
+- [x] 2.1 Give `OrderService` a `CouponRepository` dependency and wire it in `src/app.ts`; verify `npm run build` passes
+- [x] 2.2 Implement `applyCoupon(id, couponCode)` eligibility checks (order exists/pending/without coupon; coupon exists/active/within window/min amount/usage) returning the spec's error codes; verify each error case returns the expected status and code
+- [x] 2.3 Implement FIXED and PERCENT discount math with `maxDiscountCents` cap and non-negative final amount, then persist order + redemption + usage in one transaction; verify fixed, percentage, capped, and over-amount cases
+
+## 3. HTTP surface
+
+- [x] 3.1 Register `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` in `src/routes/orders.ts`, parsing the id and passing `couponCode`; verify the route returns 200 with the updated order
+
+## 4. Tests and docs
+
+- [x] 4.1 Add `tests/applyCoupon.test.ts` covering success, both discount types, cap, min amount, disabled/expired/unknown coupon, non-pending/unknown order, usage limit, and redemption/usedCount; verify `npm test` passes
+- [x] 4.2 Update `README.md` to mention the apply-coupon endpoint; verify the documented path matches the route
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the change with `openspec archive apply-coupon-to-order` once implementation is reviewed and complete.
